@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Inputs}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_RadioInputGroup}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Radio_Input_Group @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Radio_Input_Group @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</h1>
<p>
    Everything you need to work with the RadioInputGroup component: parameters, methods, models, enums, and CSS variables for styling.
</p>
<p>
    <b>Note: </b>The value updates immediately when a radio input is clicked. Unlike text-based inputs there is no <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">UpdateOnInput</span> parameter - a radio input has no
    intermediate editing state, so the bound value (on the radio input group) and validation state are always updated at the point of interaction.
</p>
<p>
    As each Input component is a single unit that contains both the input, its label and regions for both hint and error text the <b>BlazorRamp.Inputs</b> stylesheet also contains a 12 column grid layout container with
    familiar row and col classes to help with alignments. The Input component detects if its inside a Blazor Ramp <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">.br-input-row</span> and switches to using a css sub-grid to keep inputs aligned that are in adjacent
    columns. Without this, if one input was showing an error message and an input in an adjacent column was not, the heights would be different.
</p>
<p>
    The grid system employed uses a container query with common breakpoints of <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">"xs": 0px, "sm": 576px, "md": 768px, "lg": 992px, "xl": 1280px, "xxl": 1536px</span>
</p>
<p>
    The usage page shows these in action but simply add a row class on your container such as <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;div class=".br-input-row"&gt;</span> and then add the appropriate classes on the
    input directly such as <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;RadiodInputGroup class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6"&gt;</span>. For each column class/breakpoint size just add the number 1 through 12 for the
    number of columns that are spanned from the 12 fractional units to form the width.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>The input components do not define parameters for the common input attributes. You can add any of these to the Input component directly as attribute splatting will place these on the underlying input element(s).
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>Unlike some of the other components, given the browser behaviour for radio inputs, no ReadOnly or AriaDisabled parameters have been exposed. Disabling form controls is a controversial topic, but you can
    of course use attribute splatting to add whatever attribute you like to the parent container and the individual radio inputs.
</p>
<section>
    <h2 class="page-heading">
        Component parameters, methods, supporting classes and enums.
    </h2>
    <p>
        The following sections cover all components that make up this feature, including their parameters,
        public methods, and any supporting classes or enumerations required for use.
    </p>
    <section class="code-table">

        <h3 id="radio-input-group-component-parameters" class="code-table__heading">RadioInputGroup component (parent) parameters</h3>

        <table aria-labelledby="radio-input-group-component-parameters">

            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                    <th scope="col">Type</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>OptionValues</td>
                    <td>RenderFragment?</td>
                    <td>The render fragment used for the child <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;RadioInput /&gt;</span> components</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>LabelText</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the name used for to title this radio group.
                        If the value is null, empty, or whitespace then the field name is used.
                        <strong>Note: </strong>This value is captured during the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">OnInitialized</span> method
                        and changes thereafter are ignored.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ControlID</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">id</span> attribute applied to, in this instance the parent container for the radio inputs elements.
                        When null, empty, or whitespace a <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Guid</span> string is generated automatically. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed before use.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>HintText</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the hint text rendered below the title of the radio group and above the radio inputs. When set, the text is normalised so it always ends with a full stop, and is
                        associated to the radio input group via <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-describedby</span>. When null, empty, or whitespace no hint element is rendered.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Required</td>
                    <td>bool</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets whether a value for the radio input group is required. When <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">true</span>, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-required="true"</span>
                        is applied to the radio input group component and a visually hidden asterisk is appended to the title. Defaults to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">true</span>.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>ErrorsLabel</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the accessible label for the tabbable error region, used when
                        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">ValidationDisplayMode</span> is set to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">ValidationDisplayMode.TabbableWithHint</span>.
                        Defaults to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Errors</span>.
                        <strong>Note: </strong>This value is captured during the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">OnInitialized</span> method
                        and changes thereafter are ignored.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Orientation</td>
                    <td>Orientation (enum)</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the layout orientation of the radio inputs within the group.
                        Defaults to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Orientation.Horizontal</span> />.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ValidationDisplayMode</td>
                    <td>ValidationDisplayMode (enum)</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the validation display mode which controls how <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-describedby</span>
                        is set and whether the error region is tabbable. Defaults to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">ValidationDisplayMode.DescribedByWithHint</span>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>SvgIcon</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the name of a CSS custom property that resolves to an SVG data URI,
                        used as a mask-image icon alongside the tab title. Must begin with <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--</span>.
                        For example: <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--svg-my-icon</span>.
                    </td>
                </tr>

                <tr>
                    <td>AdditionalAttributes</td>
                    <td>Dictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?</td>
                    <td>
                        Sets additional attributes applied to the radio input group components root element.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Value</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>

                        Gets or sets the value of the radio input group, bound to a property on your model. Typically provided automatically when using
                        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">@@bind-Value="Model.PropertyName</span> syntax.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ValueChanged</td>
                    <td>EventCallback&lt;string&gt;></td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets a callback invoked when the bound value changes. Used for both one-way binding, where you handle the new value directly in the event callback, and two-way binding via
                        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">@@bind-Value="Model.PropertyName</span> where it is provided and managed automatically by the framework.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ValueExpression</td>
                    <td>Expression&lt;Func&lt;string&gt;&gt;</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets an expression that identifies the bound model property.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>ReadOnly</td>
                    <td>bool</td>
                    <td>
                        <strong>Note: </strong>Currently not supported, this is ignored if used.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>AriaDisabled</td>
                    <td>bool</td>
                    <td>
                        <strong>Note: </strong>Currently not supported, this is ignored if used.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>DisplayName</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Inherited from <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">InputBase&lt;TValue&gt;</span> but is <strong>not used by the Blazor Ramp inputs</strong>.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>
    <section class="code-table">

        <h3 id="radio-input-component-parameters" class="code-table__heading">RadioInput component (child) parameters</h3>

        <table aria-labelledby="radio-input-component-parameters">

            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                    <th scope="col">Type</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>LabelText</td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets or sets the name used for the radio input control label.
                        If the value is null, empty, or whitespace then the field name is used.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Value</td>
                    <td>TValue</td>
                    <td>
                        The value assigned to the radio input when checked. Should detect the parent type, but if necessary, as is the case if you want to use a nullable type
                        you would then have to specify the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">TValue</span> on each radio input.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>AdditionalAttributes</td>
                    <td>Dictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?</td>
                    <td>
                        Sets additional attributes applied to the radio input.
                    </td>
                </tr>

        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>
</section>

<section>

    <h2 class="code-table__heading">Supporting enums</h2>

    <section class="code-table">

        <h3 id="radio-input-group-orientation-enum" class="code-table__heading">Orientation enum</h3>

        <table aria-labelledby="radio-input-group-orientation-enum">

            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Value</th>
                    <th scope="col">Name</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>0</td>
                    <td>Horizontal</td>
                    <td>
                        The component uses a horizontal wrapping layout for the radio inputs
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>1</td>
                    <td>Vertical</td>
                    <td>
                        The component uses a vertically wrapping layout for the radio inputs
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>
    <section class="code-table">

        <h3 id="validation-display-mode-enum" class="code-table__heading">ValidationDisplayMode enum</h3>

        <table aria-labelledby="validation-display-mode-enum">

            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Value</th>
                    <th scope="col">Name</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>0</td>
                    <td>DescribedByWithHint</td>
                    <td>
                        Error message ID and hint text ID are both included in <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-describedby</span>.
                        Error region is not tabbable. This is the default mode.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>1</td>
                    <td>DescribedByHintSuppressed</td>
                    <td>
                        Only the error message ID is included in <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-describedby</span> when errors
                        are present, suppressing the hint text association. Error region is not tabbable.
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>2</td>
                    <td>TabbableWithHint</td>
                    <td>
                        The error region is rendered as a tabbable <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">role="region"</span> element with a
                        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">tabindex="0"</span>, allowing keyboard users to navigate directly to the errors.
                        Only the hint text ID is included in <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-describedby</span>.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

    </section>

</section>


<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>Excluding the outline offset value applied to a radio input, this Input component only uses the shared Input CSS variables as defined on the
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Inputs}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_CSS_Variables}")">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Inputs - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Shared_CSS</a> page.
    The shared outline offset variable is 0px, the radio input directly uses a value of 2px;
</p>
<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
